  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 238 AM EDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nTypical summertime pattern with SSW flow that will slowly but surely \npush temperatures back up into the low to mid 90s will for the rest \nof the forecast period; with triple digit heat index values \nreturning this weekend. Conditions are expected to flirt with heat \nadvisory criteria at the beginning of next work week. Especially the \nSE part of the CWA. \n\nFortunately, afternoon thunderstorms will be expected each afternoon \nwhich may help ease temperatures during peak heating. There is \npretty good agreement that afternoon convection will form everyday \nfor the foreseeable future. The pattern does look to change late \nnext week and into next weekend when a strong ridge sets up. The GFS \nand the CPC are hinting that a strong ridge could build some \ndangerously high temperatures into the area.",
